        <mxCell id="p1title" value="&lt;b&gt;Kacey — a turn, end to end.&lt;/b&gt; Speech never crosses the wire as audio: the browser turns voice into text and text into voice, and the socket carries JSON only. The single exception is POST /api/tts, which is still local.&lt;br/&gt;Speaking starts &lt;i&gt;before&lt;/i&gt; the reply has finished arriving — every complete sentence is spoken as soon as it is whole." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;spacing=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1020" width="1420" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
